{"grade":6,"complete":false,"main_gap":"The central estimate (7) is asserted without the necessary algebra and case split according to the sign of d(y)-d(t).","errors":[{"description":"Estimate (7), on which the constancy argument entirely depends, is not proved. It does follow by separately treating b≥c via the lower inequality and c≥b via the upper inequality, but those essential deductions are absent.","quote":"Squaring the lower and the upper inequality, rearranging, and using \(b,c\ge0\) (standard; details omitted) yields
\[
\boxed{
|d(y)-d(t)|\le \frac{(y-t)^2}{4\min\{t,y\}}.
} \tag{7}
\]"}],"notes":"Apart from this readily repairable omitted calculation, the iterate argument, partition argument, classification, and converse are correct."}
